> API and interpretation

The producer validates the complete intrinsic time grid before callbacks and
checks each actual derivative shape/value. It owns N+1 trajectory samples
whether or not optional stages are captured. Reverse and equal-endpoint
intervals are supported under the documented policy. Actual4*N calls are
measured, not a runtime or accuracy guarantee. Native Euler is a separate
executed comparison, not a report-local integrator.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

